message: "If you use this work, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Prime-Control Lattices: A Prime-Coordinate Toy Universe: Multiplicative Coding, Beat Channels, and Quantum Control"
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: Choi
    given-names: Won Sik
    email: janefather@gmail.com
version: "1.1"
date-released: 2026-08-16
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21955048
repository-code: "https://github.com/Wonsik-Choi-janefather/prime-control-lattices"
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21955048"
abstract: >-
  A self-contained mathematical toy model in which prime numbers index
  coordinate directions of a multiplicative state space. It distinguishes a
  positive-exponent monoid to select prime atoms, constructs symmetric shift
  controls with exact product-ratio and code-beat decompositions, and proves
  finite-dimensional controllability within inversion-parity sectors.
keywords:
  - prime-control lattice
  - prime-exponent lattice
  - positive-exponent monoid
  - basis gauge
  - multiplicative state space
  - quantum control
  - beat channel
  - logarithmic dynamics
